Created **[Active investigation 20: Constrained operator squares and heat flow](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/20_constrained_operator_squares/README.md)**.

It contains the [relocated research note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/20_constrained_operator_squares/notes/DIRAC_SQUARES_AND_STATIONARY_LAGUERRE_ENERGY_20261014.md), a [review of all three versions](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/20_constrained_operator_squares/reviews/THREE_SOURCE_NOTES_REVIEW_20261014.md), and a research plan with concrete tests and possible paper endpoints.

The versions reveal three related directions:

- **2017:** The heat-semigroup factorization of the Coulomb interaction into smoothed density squares is sound. The attempted implementation by conjugation needs repair; Gaussian averaging provides a suitable replacement. :codex-file-citation{path="/Users/ebbaker/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Tex/Greens_Function_Integral/Notes/10-31-17/Continuum_sigma.pdf" purpose="source"}
- **February 2018:** The imaginary-time energy identities give a particularly concrete application. Your observation that approximate evolution can lose the variational bound identifies a precise problem to solve. :codex-file-citation{path="/Users/ebbaker/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Tex/Greens_Function_Integral/Heat_Quantum/Heat_Quantum.pdf" purpose="source"}
- **August 2018:** The Dirac construction supplies operator machinery and the constrained-square idea, with some proposed identities still needing correction. :codex-file-citation{path="/Users/ebbaker/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Tex/Greens_Function_Integral/Dirac_operator_flow/Dirac_operator_flow.pdf" purpose="source"}

I also saved a **[first exact result: residual-corrected heat-trajectory identities](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/20_constrained_operator_squares/notes/RESIDUAL_CORRECTED_HEAT_TRAJECTORY_IDENTITIES_20261014.md)**. Retaining the evolution error and terminal endpoint recovers the actual Rayleigh quotient of the integrated trial state. Exact-arithmetic checks passed, including an example where omitting those terms violates the variational bound.

This gives us a concrete first use case: **error-controlled quantum-energy approximations**, alongside the more ambitious theta stationary-sign application. A paper would still need a useful new bound or demonstrated computational advantage; the project now specifies how to test for that.
